---
title: Smithy cipher
tags: tools
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
<p class="px-2">
    Smithy is interesting cipher, built using the fibonacci sequence as part of the keyword ecryption/decryption process. It was originally made for private amusement, and included in documentation in The Da Vinci Code copyright case. For example: 
    <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">Hello</code> encrypted with a key of <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">World</code> would shift like: 
    <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">Rmxsp</code> 
</p>
<p class="px-2">
    There is more information available on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithy_code" class="text-convrtr">{{
        filename | capitalize }}</a> Wikipedia page
</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Smithy cipher", placeholder = "Example: Hello &srarr; World [key] &srarr; Rmxsp") %}
<div class="input-group w-auto">
    <label class="input-group-text" for="{{ filename }}Key"><span class="visually-hidden">Smithy </span>Key</label>
    <input type="text" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Key" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
    <button class="btn btn-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Encrypt" aria-pressed="true">Encrypt</button>
    <button class="btn btn-outline-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Decrypt" aria-pressed="false">Decrypt</button>
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
